1. **Sub-population Definition**: Tracers are divided into "Strain-dominated" (spending >70% of their time in strain regions) and "Vortex-dominated" (<30% time in strain regions) based on the previously computed strain percentages.
2. **MSD and Hurst Exponent**: The Mean Squared Displacement (MSD) and the running Hurst exponent H(t) are computed for these sub-populations independently to compare their transport properties and isolate the effect of the strain field.
3. **Lagrangian Velocities**: The velocity components vx(t) and vy(t) are computed using forward finite differences of the unwrapped trajectories. The units are length/time.
4. **Velocity Autocorrelation**: The Lagrangian velocity autocorrelation function Rv(tau) is computed using Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) for efficiency. The decorrelation time (in time units) is estimated by integrating Rv(tau) up to its first zero-crossing.
5. **Velocity Increments PDF**: The probability density functions (PDFs) of the Lagrangian velocity increments delta v(tau) are computed at multiple lags (10, 100, 500).
